{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-33466","model_call":23,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3378"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3378"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1342244096#1_2785327046","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3378","rank":4,"snippet":"provides key takeaways that allow the project manager to coach effectively without authority and increase the chance of successful team performance. From this paper, a project manager will develop an understanding of what coaching is and how it compares to mentoring and training, and will review why coaching is important in the context of project teams. The questions of who to coach and when and where to engage in coaching provide the project manager coach with guidance on looking for opportunities to <cover>improve team outcomes through coaching. Finally, the project manager will review various methods of coaching and learn the phases of a coaching engagement, followed by guidelines on how to determine the success of the coaching engagement. Introduction Success in today’s business community requires a high level of effort to achieve goals that align with strategic organizational objectives. Many business leaders focus on professional development to ensure their continued successful performance.\" , \"start_char\": 388.000000 , \"title\": \"Project Manager as Team Coach - </cover>Plan for Success\" , \"url\": \"https://www.pmi.org/learning/library/project-manager-team-coach-plan-success-6251\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1350642059#2_3126844754","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1350642059#1_3126842540","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1350642059#4_3126848652","rank":3,"relevance":3}]},"time":7},"model_calls":23,"document_judgments":14,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
