{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-33466","model_call":58,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ coach trust \"team performance\" athletes)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ coach trust \"team performance\" athletes)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1364749777#15_2865845666","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3404","rank":1,"snippet":"Image On Your Site \" , \"segment\": \"You’re teaching them that there aren’t excuses, and anything is possible with hard work. 10) Learn to Be a Good Leader Coaches are leaders. While you have to learn to motivate and push your athletes, you have to learn to lead and inspire them too. To improve <cover>team performance, study greats like Abraham Lincoln, Martin Luther King Jr, Winston Churchill, or other leaders that personally inspire you. Learn the values that make a good leader, and work to exemplify them. You’ll be a role model for your athletes, and you’ll encourage them to be better people too. Also, make sure you don’t lose your team. They should have full confidence in you, as their coach. 11) Understand Limits To earn your player’s trust, </cover>you need to build a history of pushing them hard, but not harder than they can handle. Learn to understand your player’s limits and create a history that they can trust you.\" , \"start_char\": 6116.000000 , \"title\": \"14 Ways For Coaches To Improve Team Performance!\" ,"},"time":81},"model_calls":58,"document_judgments":41,"relevance_3":13,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
